"""
Tests for B6 hybrid multi-signal retrieval: BM25 lexical arm + RRF fusion.

Covers the plan's T1-T12 (see the numbered test classes):
  T1-T3  BM25 properties (IDF, TF saturation, length normalization)
  T4     tokenizer behavior (case, NFKC, whole-token, empty)
  T5     RRF fusion ordering + deterministic tiebreaks
  T6     adversarial ranking regression (T6a broad-coverage stuffing beats
         the legacy scorer and is defeated by BM25; T6b BM25's introduced
         TF sensitivity is bounded)
  T7     measured-gain pin: BM25 strictly beats legacy binary-presence on
         MRR and P@3 over the labeled fixture (values pinned)
  T8     kill switch LEXICAL_RANKING_ENABLED: flag-off is byte-identical to
         the legacy algorithm (independent reimplementation), garbage
         values follow the falsy-list parse (unset/garbage => ON)
  T10    filter classes: where-filtered docs never appear regardless of
         BM25 score (pre-rank impossibility)
  T11    scoped-IDF invariant: flooding one owner scope leaves another
         scope's ranking identical
  T12    membership/total: zero-match queries return empty results under
         both flag states; no zero-arm filler

T9 (retriever-layer hash-embedding gate) lives in test_learning_hygiene.py
next to the invariants it updates.

The MEASURED-GAIN NUMBERS pinned in T7 are fixture-scale measurements, not
benchmark claims -- see GOVERNANCE Non-Claims.
"""

import pytest

from {{ project_slug }}.learning.rag.lexical import (
    bm25_scores,
